WEBVTT

00:59:29.322 --> 00:59:31.861
And you look back, they were
complaining in the 1950s.

00:59:31.885 --> 00:59:33.568
Well ... things were okay. (Laughs)

00:59:33.592 --> 00:59:36.714
And in retrospect, most
of the cataclysms never come to pass.

00:59:36.738 --> 00:59:38.909
We in the public intellectual business

00:59:38.933 --> 00:59:41.336
are cataclysmic because
it wins us attention,

00:59:41.360 --> 00:59:44.224
and because we genuinely
want to draw attention to problems.

00:59:44.248 --> 00:59:46.518
But, if you look at
the balance of our history,

00:59:46.542 --> 00:59:48.857
it's the story of people
suffering through things

00:59:48.881 --> 00:59:50.218
and then figuring it out.

00:59:50.242 --> 00:59:51.979
And that was true of the Civil War,

00:59:52.003 --> 00:59:54.280
which was a more tumultuous
period than our own.

00:59:54.304 --> 00:59:56.704
It was true of World War II,
the Great Depression.

00:59:56.728 --> 00:59:58.752
These were all worse periods than our own.

00:59:58.776 --> 01:00:01.182
What decade, exactly,
do people want to go back to?